// nvHASH web tier — Prisma multi-file schema for the `app` domain (app-spec
// §3 decision 3, §9.1; ADR-001 Decision 1). One model per `prisma/*.prisma`
// file (the indexer/nuva precedent). Every table lives in the `app` Postgres
// schema, owned by the `app_writer` role — which has NO grants on `indexed`
// (roles.sql; asserted by the standing grant-boundary gate). Indexed history
// is read only through services/api.
//
// Data minimization (SECURITY.md; app-spec §12.3): the `app` schema holds
// sessions, single-use login nonces, and the accepted per-address first/last
// seen timestamps — nothing else in PR 5.1. No role column anywhere (roles
// are live on-chain facts re-checked per refresh, never persisted — spec §4),
// no IP or device identifiers, no off-chain identity. Enforced, not trusted,
// by the schema-field allowlist gate (test/app-schema-allowlist.test.ts).
// Adding a column is a design-review event: it must be added to the allowlist,
// not merely to a migration.

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
  schemas  = ["app"]
}

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}
